---
// WHAT WE HANDLE — built 2026-08-25 to docs/ASEPTACLEAN-CODEX-HOMEPAGE-BRIEF-V3-LEAN-SEVENSON.md
// §10. This ONE section replaces BOTH of the sections it supersedes:
//
//   ConditionRecognition ("What are you dealing with?")  — the recognition/routing section
//   ServiceFeatures      ("What Aseptaclean handles now.") — the long services section
//
// §10's reasoning, which is the whole point of the merge: the homepage does not need two
// separate routing systems for the same idea. The audited page ran both, one after the other,
// at a combined 3,374px on desktop and 5,202px at 390px — and they routed to overlapping sets
// of the same service pages. One photographic section now does both jobs: "that looks like my
// situation" and "yes, Aseptaclean handles this kind of problem."
//
// WHAT WAS CUT, deliberately, per §10's copy rule (title + one sentence + one link):
//   · the three multi-paragraph service essays, including the three "why routine cleaning does
//     not fit" paragraphs written for the previous brief;
//   · the eleven-row written-checklist panel (still on /detailed-cleaning/ and the deep-cleaning
//     page, which is where a checklist answers a question someone is actually asking);
//   · the second tier of per-family route grids, replaced by one plain "More services" row —
//     §10: "Do not create another card grid."
//
// `id="service-cards"` IS CARRIED OVER for the third time and must stay. /about/ and /404/ both
// link to `/#service-cards`. The section that originally owned the anchor is long gone; the
// destination it means is this one, so the anchor travels with the content rather than becoming
// two dead links.
//
// GATED ROUTES CANNOT BE LINKED FROM THIS FILE. Every href is filtered through each service
// record's own `indexable` flag, exactly as ServiceFeatures did. Post-construction, window,
// eviction, animal-waste, rodent, pigeon and commercial all fail the filter today and drop out
// on their own; /specialty-cleaning/ is noindex and is not referenced. Clearing doc 27 §21 and
// the B&P §8550(a) constraint is the unblock — not editing this file. This also keeps `/`, which
// is indexable, from creating an indexable→noindex crawl path (release-checklist C10).
//
// THE ANIMAL / ORGANIC FAMILY IS NOT A ROUTE HERE. Its only route,
// /animal-waste-cleanup-san-jose/, ships noindex, and §10 says outright "Do not expose gated
// services." The family is therefore not described in this section, which is also why
// docs/21-CLAIMS-AND-COMPLIANCE-LAW.md §2.3's verbatim limiting clause does not appear in it:
// §2.3 binds "wherever animal or organic condition work is described", and this section does not
// describe it. The clause still travels with the family everywhere it IS described — it is part
// of the homepage.serviceCards string itself, including inside the Service JSON-LD `/` emits.
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import hoardingImage from "../assets/homepage/condition-development-hoarding-asurnipal.jpg";
import neglectedImage from "../assets/homepage/condition-development-neglected-kolforn.jpg";
import resetImage from "../assets/homepage/condition-development-reset-aismallard.jpg";
import serviceImage from "../assets/homepage/service-development-cleanup-asurnipal.jpg";

// TEMPORARY DEVELOPMENT REFERENCE PHOTOGRAPHS — NOT Aseptaclean project work, not proof of any
// completed job, and not client properties. All three are `[ATMOS]`-class under the image rule in
// docs/21-CLAIMS-AND-COMPLIANCE-LAW.md §6: no crew, no technician, no equipment, no document and
// no before/after pair, so none of them implies Aseptaclean performed the work. §6 caps
// atmosphere imagery at three slots; V3 §19 supersedes that cap for homepage development only,
// so the composition can be judged before the owner shoot — it is NOT permission to present any
// of these as proof. Replace all three with owner-shot photography before launch
// (docs/06-ASSET-MANIFEST.md §5).
//
//   condition-development-hoarding-asurnipal.jpg
//     Asurnipal — CC BY-SA 4.0
//     https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bregenz-Cluttered_interiors_(compulsive_hoarding)-living_room-02ASD.jpg
//   condition-development-neglected-kolforn.jpg
//     Kolforn — CC BY-SA 4.0
//     https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2_Church_Cottage_West_Runton_30_01_2010_(14).JPG
//   condition-development-reset-aismallard.jpg
//     aismallard — CC BY-SA 3.0
//     https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empty_apartment_room_with_corner_windows.jpg

// Locked copy's exact four doors — docs/aseptaclean-all-website-copy.md, "What are you dealing
// with?" — one per public service route.
const situations = [
  {
    slug: "contents",
    title: "Found rodent droppings or animal waste?",
    detail:
      "Droppings, urine, nesting material, animal waste, odors, or affected areas after pest activity may need more than a quick sweep or surface clean.",
    detailTwo: "Aseptaclean handles the cleanup side after rodent or animal activity.",
    linkLabel: "Rodent Droppings & Animal Waste Cleanup",
    href: "/rodent-dropping-cleanup-san-jose/",
    image: serviceImage,
    alt: "Reference photograph of an affected area requiring specialty cleanup."
  },
  {
    slug: "neglected",
    title: "Has the home become difficult to manage?",
    detail:
      "Heavy clutter, accumulated belongings, blocked rooms, trash mixed with personal items, or years of contents can make it hard to know where to begin.",
    detailTwo:
      "We help break the property into clear steps so the work can move forward without treating everything inside as disposable.",
    linkLabel: "Hoarding Cleanup",
    href: "/hoarding-cleanup-san-jose/",
    image: hoardingImage,
    alt: "Reference photograph of a living room where accumulated household contents cover the floor and furniture."
  },
  {
    slug: "transition",
    title: "Has the property gone beyond a normal deep clean?",
    detail:
      "Heavy buildup, trash, animal waste, strong odors, neglected rooms, heavily soiled kitchens or bathrooms, and difficult sanitation conditions can change the job completely.",
    detailTwo: "These properties need a cleanup plan built around their actual condition.",
    linkLabel: "Severe Property Cleanup",
    href: "/extreme-cleaning-san-jose/",
    image: neglectedImage,
    alt: "Reference photograph of a neglected residential kitchen with worn, long-unmaintained surfaces."
  },
  {
    slug: "detail",
    title: "Does the home need much more detail than routine cleaning?",
    detail:
      "Some homes are not severely affected. They simply need more time, more hand work, and more attention than a normal cleaning appointment allows.",
    detailTwo:
      "Aseptaclean provides detailed one-time cleaning for major home resets, move-in preparation, move-out preparation, and properties with heavy kitchen, bathroom, or whole-home buildup.",
    linkLabel: "Detailed Deep Cleaning",
    href: "/deep-cleaning-san-jose/",
    image: resetImage,
    alt: "Reference photograph of an emptied residential room with bare walls and a clean wood floor."
  }
] as const;

---

<section class="handle" id="service-cards" aria-labelledby="handle-title">
  <div class="handle__inner">
    <header class="handle__header">
      <h2 id="handle-title" class="ac-type-h2-home-feature">What are you dealing with?</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need to know the name of the service before you contact us. Start with what
        is happening at the property.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="handle__routes">
      {situations.map((situation) => (
        <article class={`route route--${situation.slug}`}>
          <div class="route__media">
            <Image
              src={situation.image}
              alt={situation.alt}
              widths={[420, 620, 840, 1100]}
              sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 23vw, (min-width: 40rem) 46vw, 92vw"
              format="webp"
              quality={76}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="route__copy">
            <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-route">{situation.title}</h3>
            <p>{situation.detail}</p>
            <p>{situation.detailTwo}</p>
            {/* Exactly one link per item, stretched over the whole article so the photograph is
                clickable without adding a second anchor to the same destination. The heading is
                deliberately NOT a link — two anchors to one route is what §10's "one simple text
                link" rules out. */}
            <a class="route__link" href={situation.href}>
              {situation.linkLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <nav class="handle__more" aria-label="More services">
      <a href="/services/">All current services</a>
    </nav>

    <p class="handle__development-note">
      Development reference photographs · not Aseptaclean project work · Wikimedia Commons,
      CC BY-SA
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .handle {
    background: var(--ac-color-paper);
    padding-block: clamp(76px, 7.5vw, 112px);
  }

  .handle__inner {
    width: min(100% - 64px, 1320px);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* V3 §23 caps homepage H2s at 36–42px; the audited build ran 52px. 40px (2.5rem) is the value
     used by all three surviving H2s, set on the token rather than on the heading so AGENTS.md §6
     law 1 holds — the size still resolves through .ac-type-h2-home-feature. */
  .handle__header {
    --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 4vw, 60px);
  }

  /* 56ch, not 40: at 40 the line broke after "before" and left the supporting sentence stacked
     in a narrow column under a one-line heading, with the rest of a 1320px row empty. One line
     at desktop reads as a caption to the heading, which is what it is. */
  .handle__header p {
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-600);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .handle__routes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 32px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .route {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* 4:5 portrait, not the old 1:1 thumbnail. §10 asks for images that "feel important, not
     thumbnails"; at a 1320px container each panel is ~418px wide and ~522px tall, which is the
     tallest element in the section and makes photography, not type, carry it. */
  .route__media {
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    background: var(--ac-color-steel-200);
  }

  .route__media :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 160ms ease;
  }

  /* Each photograph carries its subject in a different part of the frame, so the focal point is
     tuned per panel rather than shared. */
  .route--contents .route__media :global(img) {
    object-position: 50% 58%;
  }

  .route--neglected .route__media :global(img) {
    object-position: 46% 52%;
  }

  .route--transition .route__media :global(img) {
    object-position: 58% 56%;
  }

  .route--detail .route__media :global(img) {
    object-position: 50% 50%;
  }

  .route:hover .route__media :global(img) {
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }

  .route__copy {
    display: flex;
    flex: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ac-color-navy-800);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .route__copy h3 {
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .route__copy p {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-600);
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Panels are equal-height grid items, so pushing the link to the bottom aligns all three
     without reserving a fixed number of description lines. */
  .route__link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-800);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .route__link::after {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    inset: 0;
    content: "";
  }

  .route:hover .route__link {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .route__link:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ac-color-navy-800);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* §10's secondary treatment: one hairline row of plain text links. No cards, no icons, no
     second grid. */
  .handle__more {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ac-color-line-strong);
    margin-top: clamp(40px, 4vw, 56px);
    padding-top: 18px;
    gap: 4px 26px;
  }

  .handle__more > span {
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .handle__more a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-600);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .handle__more a:hover {
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
  }

  .handle__more a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ac-color-navy-800);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .handle__development-note {
    /* Same opt-out as the hero's disclaimer, 2026-08-26, and the same reason: global.css's
       `:where(p, li)` 62ch prose measure resolves to ~455px at this 11px size, which broke a
       one-line credit into two inside a 1320px container. The cap is right for prose and wrong
       for a caption. This one wrapped rather than clipped, so it stayed legible — it is
       corrected here because it is the same disclaimer doing the same job. */
    max-width: none;
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-400);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.055em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  @media (max-width: 64rem) {
    .handle__inner {
      width: min(100% - 52px, 1320px);
    }

    .handle__header {
      --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2.25rem;
    }

    .handle__routes {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .handle {
      padding-block: 64px;
    }

    .handle__inner {
      width: calc(100% - 40px);
    }

    .handle__header {
      --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .handle__header p {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .handle__routes {
      gap: 40px;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .route__media {
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .route__media :global(img),
    .route:hover .route__media :global(img) {
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
